-- title:
--   X Evaluated Full Slice ABABAvg To X Evaluated Full Slice ABABtensor Avg
-- statement:
--   **The x-evaluated scalar quartic is close to its full-slice tensor form.**
--
--   Let $(q,m,d)$ have a field model, let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the successor space, and let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family. Assume that the state is normalized and that `family` is strongly self-consistent in $S$ with error $\zeta$. Then the x-evaluated full-slice scalar $\mathrm{ABAB}$ average and its x-evaluated tensor average differ by at most
--
--   $$
--   \left|
--   \mathrm{xEvaluatedFullSliceABABAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})
--   -\mathrm{xEvaluatedFullSliceABABtensorAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})
--   \right|
--   \le \sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The result is the scalar-to-tensor comparison for the x-evaluated full-slice endpoint. It supplies a component of the transport chain used by `fullSlice_scalar_marginalize_y`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.xEvaluatedFullSliceABABAvg_to_xEvaluatedFullSliceABABtensorAvg`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
